# ── App-store signing material ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Added 2026-09-04, after the owner generated the Android upload keystore and
# the iOS signing request INTO THE REPOSITORY ROOT and `git status` listed all
# three as untracked. Nothing was committed, which is the only reason this is a
# one-line fix: a signing key in git history cannot be un-published, and for
# the Android upload key it is unrecoverable in a worse sense — Play ties the
# app to that key forever, so a leak means the listing can never be updated
# safely again.
#
# Verified before adding: `git ls-files` matches NONE of these patterns, so no
# tracked file is silently dropped from the index by them.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: `google-services.json` and `GoogleService-Info.plist`.
# They are FCM configuration rather than secrets, the native build needs them
# committed to work, and ignoring them would create exactly the failure this
# repository keeps meeting — a file present on disk, absent from the build, and
# nothing anywhere saying so.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.p8
*.mobileprovision
*.certSigningRequest
ios_distribution.key
